# Custom DRC rules: HV Pi Hat (5 kV DEA driver)
# Auto-loaded by KiCad/pcbnew because this file is named "<project>.kicad_dru".
#
# HV nets are in netclass HV_5kV (rail, per-channel outputs, discharge nodes), bound by the
# .kicad_pro pattern /HV_* . Netclass HV_Return currently has no nets.
#
# Layer strategy (docs/adr/0002-hv-on-outer-layers.md): HV copper on F.Cu and B.Cu only; In1/In2
# carry rule-area keepouts under the HV zone. The 2-D rules below cannot see through-board spacing;
# check that with tools/HvInterlayer.py.
#
# PROVISIONAL VALUES. The 2 mm figures below have no accepted basis. IEC 60664-1:2020 gives 20 mm
# creepage (Table F.5, pollution degree 1) and 5.7 mm clearance (Table F.8, 5 kV peak, inhomogeneous)
# for a coated board; see docs/adr/0003-hv-spacing-basis.md. Rev A fails those by 354 violations.
# These rules stay at 2 mm only so DRC keeps checking connectivity and relative spacing until
# ADR-0003 is decided. Do not fabricate against them.
(version 1)

(rule "HV surface creepage"
	(constraint creepage (min 2mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'HV_5kV' || A.NetClass == 'HV_Return'"))

(rule "HV air clearance"
	(constraint clearance (min 2mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'HV_5kV' || A.NetClass == 'HV_Return'"))

# The GND guard pour keeps 4 mm from HV: it is a large coplanar plane next to every HV net.
(rule "HV to GND pour"
	(constraint clearance (min 4mm))
	(condition "(A.NetClass == 'HV_5kV' || A.NetClass == 'HV_Return') && B.Type == 'Zone'"))

# HV copper keeps 1 mm from any drilled hole (hole_clearance is a same-layer copper-to-hole rule;
# it does not check through-board spacing).
(rule "HV interlayer hole/pad spacing"
	(constraint hole_clearance (min 1mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'HV_5kV' || A.NetClass == 'HV_Return'"))
